From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:44:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 121/159] [ae-patch] Fold the phone session menu's Status and
 Move items under one row each

omnigent-ae patch 0121 (2026-10-20). On a phone the sidebar session menu
listed every Status value and every Move item inline under headings,
about 20 rows, and ran off the bottom of the screen. Status and Move are
now one row each (new web/src/shell/AeMenuFold.tsx): the label, the
current value (Status shows the stored one with its icon) and a chevron.
Tapping the row shows or hides its items in place under it, in a tinted
block, and keeps the menu open; picking an item still closes it. Desktop
keeps its side flyouts unchanged.

Tests: the mobile cases in AeStatusMenu.test.tsx, Sidebar.aeStatus.test.tsx
and Sidebar.aeSortModes.test.tsx open the fold row before reading the
items, and check it starts shut, reports aria-expanded and shuts again.
